{"version_id": 33, "article_id": 4, "level_code": "en_b1", "lang": "en", "level": 3, "level_label": "B1 中级", "title": "Ex-German spy chief arrested for treason and spying", "title_zh": "德国前情报局长因叛国和间谍罪被捕", "topic": "world", "source": "bbc_world", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c58jzyer1kr0o?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(230, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(268, 46%, 48%)", "label": "WORLD", "seed": "cf9eb2e77a6c"}, "published_date": "2026-10-06", "word_count": 278, "reading_minutes": 1.4, "lead": "A former head of Germany's intelligence service has been arrested. Prosecutors say he passed secret information to foreign spies.", "lead_zh": "德国情报机构前负责人已被逮捕。检察官称他向外国间谍传递了秘密信息。", "preview": "August Hanning, who led the Federal Intelligence Service (BND) from 1998 to 2005, was arrested on suspicion of espionage and treason. After ", "preview_zh": "奥古斯特·汉宁曾于1998年至2005年领导德国联邦情报局（BND），他因涉嫌间谍活动和叛国罪被捕。离开BND后，他担任私人顾问。检察官称，他利用机密情报为一家外国间谍机构撰写分析报告，并且还与另一家外国机构保持联系。然而，调查人员没有透露涉及哪些国家。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 23, "url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@2753ccc/content/audio/4/en_b1.mp3", "duration": 115.65, "size_bytes": 697680, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural", "word_count": 311, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@2753ccc/content/data/versions/33.json", "paragraphs": ["August Hanning, who led the Federal Intelligence Service (BND) from 1998 to 2005, was arrested on suspicion of espionage and treason. After leaving the BND, he worked as a private consultant. Prosecutors say he used classified intelligence to write an analysis for a foreign spy service, and he also stayed in contact with another foreign service. However, investigators have not said which countries were involved.", "Police also arrested a former BND employee called Manfred D. They accuse him of giving Hanning about 2,000 classified documents in exchange for money. Manfred D was Hanning's bureau chief and stayed in the BND until this year. He is charged with helping with attempted treason and treasonous espionage. Hanning was arrested at his home in Nordwalde, while Manfred D was arrested in Bavaria.", "Prosecutors say Manfred D used his position to get highly confidential information. Between 2012 and 2026, he also worked as chief of staff for Hanning's successors. The findings suggest that over the years he gave Hanning about 2,000 documents, many with classified information meant only for the BND. On one occasion, Hanning used this material to write an analysis for a foreign intelligence officer, though it is unclear if it reached the right person.", "Hanning is also accused of being in close contact with a representative of another foreign service for several years. He allegedly passed on political information, partly based on documents from Manfred D. Local media report that the case came to light during a separate investigation into Christina Block, a German steakhouse heiress. Police reportedly found an electronic storage device with sensitive BND documents. Hanning denies any wrongdoing, and he is due in court on Wednesday."], "paragraphs_zh": ["奥古斯特·汉宁曾于1998年至2005年领导德国联邦情报局（BND），他因涉嫌间谍活动和叛国罪被捕。离开BND后，他担任私人顾问。检察官称，他利用机密情报为一家外国间谍机构撰写分析报告，并且还与另一家外国机构保持联系。然而，调查人员没有透露涉及哪些国家。", "警方还逮捕了一名前BND雇员，名叫曼弗雷德·D。他们指控他向汉宁提供了约2000份机密文件，以换取金钱。曼弗雷德·D曾是汉宁的办公室主任，并一直在BND工作到今年。他被控协助未遂叛国和叛国间谍活动。汉宁在诺德瓦尔德家中被捕，而曼弗雷德·D在巴伐利亚被捕。", "检察官称，曼弗雷德·D利用职务之便获取了高度机密信息。2012年至2026年间，他还担任汉宁继任者的幕僚长。调查结果表明，多年来他向汉宁提供了约2000份文件，其中许多包含仅供BND内部使用的机密信息。有一次，汉宁利用这些材料为一名外国情报官员撰写分析报告，但目前不清楚材料是否送达了目标对象。", "汉宁还被指控多年来与另一家外国机构的代表保持密切联系。据称，他传递了政治信息，部分基于曼弗雷德·D提供的文件。当地媒体报道称，此案是在对德国牛排连锁店女继承人克里斯蒂娜·布洛克进行另一起调查时曝光的。据报道，警方发现了一个存有敏感BND文件的电子存储设备。汉宁否认有任何不当行为，他将于周三出庭。"], "body": "August Hanning, who led the Federal Intelligence Service (BND) from 1998 to 2005, was arrested on suspicion of espionage and treason. After leaving the BND, he worked as a private consultant. Prosecutors say he used classified intelligence to write an analysis for a foreign spy service, and he also stayed in contact with another foreign service. However, investigators have not said which countries were involved.\n\nPolice also arrested a former BND employee called Manfred D. They accuse him of giving Hanning about 2,000 classified documents in exchange for money. Manfred D was Hanning's bureau chief and stayed in the BND until this year. He is charged with helping with attempted treason and treasonous espionage. Hanning was arrested at his home in Nordwalde, while Manfred D was arrested in Bavaria.\n\nProsecutors say Manfred D used his position to get highly confidential information. Between 2012 and 2026, he also worked as chief of staff for Hanning's successors. The findings suggest that over the years he gave Hanning about 2,000 documents, many with classified information meant only for the BND. On one occasion, Hanning used this material to write an analysis for a foreign intelligence officer, though it is unclear if it reached the right person.\n\nHanning is also accused of being in close contact with a representative of another foreign service for several years. He allegedly passed on political information, partly based on documents from Manfred D. Local media report that the case came to light during a separate investigation into Christina Block, a German steakhouse heiress. Police reportedly found an electronic storage device with sensitive BND documents. Hanning denies any wrongdoing, and he is due in court on Wednesday.", "body_zh": "奥古斯特·汉宁曾于1998年至2005年领导德国联邦情报局（BND），他因涉嫌间谍活动和叛国罪被捕。离开BND后，他担任私人顾问。检察官称，他利用机密情报为一家外国间谍机构撰写分析报告，并且还与另一家外国机构保持联系。然而，调查人员没有透露涉及哪些国家。\n\n警方还逮捕了一名前BND雇员，名叫曼弗雷德·D。他们指控他向汉宁提供了约2000份机密文件，以换取金钱。曼弗雷德·D曾是汉宁的办公室主任，并一直在BND工作到今年。他被控协助未遂叛国和叛国间谍活动。汉宁在诺德瓦尔德家中被捕，而曼弗雷德·D在巴伐利亚被捕。\n\n检察官称，曼弗雷德·D利用职务之便获取了高度机密信息。2012年至2026年间，他还担任汉宁继任者的幕僚长。调查结果表明，多年来他向汉宁提供了约2000份文件，其中许多包含仅供BND内部使用的机密信息。有一次，汉宁利用这些材料为一名外国情报官员撰写分析报告，但目前不清楚材料是否送达了目标对象。\n\n汉宁还被指控多年来与另一家外国机构的代表保持密切联系。据称，他传递了政治信息，部分基于曼弗雷德·D提供的文件。当地媒体报道称，此案是在对德国牛排连锁店女继承人克里斯蒂娜·布洛克进行另一起调查时曝光的。据报道，警方发现了一个存有敏感BND文件的电子存储设备。汉宁否认有任何不当行为，他将于周三出庭。", "text": "August Hanning, who led the Federal Intelligence Service (BND) from 1998 to 2005, was arrested on suspicion of espionage and treason. After leaving the BND, he worked as a private consultant. Prosecutors say he used classified intelligence to write an analysis for a foreign spy service, and he also stayed in contact with another foreign service. However, investigators have not said which countries were involved. Police also arrested a former BND employee called Manfred D. They accuse him of giving Hanning about 2,000 classified documents in exchange for money. Manfred D was Hanning's bureau chief and stayed in the BND until this year. He is charged with helping with attempted treason and treasonous espionage. Hanning was arrested at his home in Nordwalde, while Manfred D was arrested in Bavaria. Prosecutors say Manfred D used his position to get highly confidential information. Between 2012 and 2026, he also worked as chief of staff for Hanning's successors. The findings suggest that over the years he gave Hanning about 2,000 documents, many with classified information meant only for the BND. On one occasion, Hanning used this material to write an analysis for a foreign intelligence officer, though it is unclear if it reached the right person. Hanning is also accused of being in close contact with a representative of another foreign service for several years. He allegedly passed on political information, partly based on documents from Manfred D. Local media report that the case came to light during a separate investigation into Christina Block, a German steakhouse heiress. Police reportedly found an electronic storage device with sensitive BND documents. Hanning denies any wrongdoing, and he is due in court on Wednesday.", "vocab": [{"word": "espionage", "pos": "noun", "zh": "间谍活动", "note": "常指国家层面的间谍行为，比 spying 更正式"}, {"word": "treason", "pos": "noun", "zh": "叛国罪", "note": "法律用语，指背叛国家的行为"}, {"word": "classified", "pos": "adj", "zh": "机密的", "note": "常修饰 information、documents 等"}, {"word": "prosecutor", "pos": "noun", "zh": "检察官", "note": "负责提起公诉的官员"}, {"word": "allege", "pos": "verb", "zh": "指控；声称", "note": "常用于被动语态，表示未经证实的说法"}, {"word": "confidential", "pos": "adj", "zh": "保密的", "note": "强调不公开、仅限于特定人员"}, {"word": "in exchange for", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "作为交换", "note": "后接名词，表示交换条件"}, {"word": "come to light", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "曝光；被发现", "note": "常用短语，指事情被揭露"}, {"word": "deny", "pos": "verb", "zh": "否认", "note": "后接名词或动名词，如 deny doing sth"}, {"word": "due in court", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "出庭受审", "note": "表示按计划要出庭"}], "title_original": "Former German spy chief arrested for espionage and treason", "summary_original": "August Hanning is accused of obtaining classified information for a foreign power.", "body_original": "Former German spy chief arrested for espionage and treason\nBy\nOlivia Ireland\nPublished\n6 hours ago\nFormer German spy chief August Hanning has been arrested on suspicion of espionage, treason and obtaining classified information for a foreign power, the German Federal Prosecutor's Office says.\nHanning headed the Federal Intelligence Service (BND) from 1998 to 2005 and has since been working as a private consultant.\nProsecutors allege that he used classified intelligence to \"draft an analysis\" for one foreign intelligence service and maintained contact with another foreign spying service. Investigators have not disclosed which foreign powers were involved.\nPolice also arrested former BND employee Manfred D, accusing him of passing Hanning about 2,000 classified documents for money.\nManfred D, who was Hanning's bureau chief and remained in the BND until this year, is charged with aiding and abetting attempted treason and treasonous espionage.\nLocal media reported Hanning was arrested at his home in Nordwalde near Münster while Manfred D was arrested in Bavaria. Hanning is due in court on Wednesday and Manfred D will appear on Tuesday.\nProsecutors say Manfred D, who also served as the chief of staff for Hanning's successors between 2012 and 2026, used his role to gain access to highly confidential information which he then passed on to Hanning \"in exchange for remuneration\".\n\"The current findings suggest that, over the years, Manfred D provided Hanning with approximately 2,000 documents, many of which contained classified information to be used exclusively by the Federal Intelligence Service for internal purposes,\" the statement says.\n\"On one occasion, Hanning used classified intelligence ... to draft an analysis for an officer of a foreign intelligence service,\" prosecutors said, noting it was not clear if \"the material reached the intended recipient\".\nHanning is also accused of being \"in close contact with a representative of another foreign intelligence service, to whom he passed on political information, partially based on material provided by Manfred D, for several years\".\nLocal media say Hanning's alleged possession of intelligence documents came to light during a separate case relating to German steakhouse heiress Christina Block.\nHamburg public prosecutor's office accused Block of orchestrating the kidnapping of her two youngest children in 2023 due to a custody dispute. Investigators allege Hanning was involved in an earlier attempted kidnapping of the children, which he denies.\nState criminal police officers reportedly discovered an electronic data storage device containing sensitive information including recent BND documents.\nIt is not the first time the BND has faced similar controversy. A high-ranking German intelligence officer was\ncharged with treason in 2023\nfor allegedly passing state secrets to Russia.\nProsecutors alleged Carsten L shared intelligence about the war in Ukraine and the Wagner mercenary group and received roughly €400,000 ($450,000; £340,000). His trial is ongoing.\nRelated topics\nGermany\nCorruption\nSpying\nMore on this story\nAlmost 60,000 far-right extremists in Germany, intelligence agency says\nPublished\n30 June\nGermany investigates Russia links to weapons cache discovered in woods, reports say\nPublished\n21 August", "fetched_at": "2026-10-06T16:39:02.526512+00:00", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "August", "s": 0.1, "e": 0.512, "sm": 100, "em": 512, "cs": 0, "ce": 6, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "Hanning", "s": 0.525, "e": 0.913, "sm": 525, "em": 912, "cs": 7, "ce": 14, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": ",", "s": 0.913, "e": 1.15, "sm": 912, "em": 1150, "cs": 14, "ce": 15, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "who", "s": 1.15, "e": 1.25, "sm": 1150, "em": 1250, "cs": 16, "ce": 19, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "led", "s": 1.262, "e": 1.5, "sm": 1262, "em": 1500, "cs": 20, "ce": 23, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "the", "s": 1.512, "e": 1.6, "sm": 1512, "em": 1599, "cs": 24, "ce": 27, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "Federal", "s": 1.613, "e": 1.962, "sm": 1612, "em": 1962, "cs": 28, "ce": 35, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": "Intelligence", "s": 1.975, "e": 2.625, "sm": 1975, "em": 2625, "cs": 36, "ce": 48, "si": 0}, {"i": 8, "w": "Service", "s": 2.638, "e": 3.075, "sm": 2637, "em": 3075, "cs": 49, "ce": 56, "si": 0}, {"i": 9, "w": "(", "s": 3.075, "e": 3.25, "sm": 3075, "em": 3250, "cs": 57, "ce": 58, "si": 0}, {"i": 10, "w": "BND", "s": 3.25, "e": 3.9, "sm": 3250, "em": 3900, "cs": 58, "ce": 61, "si": 0}, {"i": 11, "w": ")", "s": 3.9, "e": 4.15, "sm": 3900, "em": 4150, "cs": 61, "ce": 62, "si": 0}, {"i": 12, "w": "from", "s": 4.15, "e": 4.807, "sm": 4150, "em": 4807, "cs": 63, "ce": 67, "si": 0}, {"i": 13, "w": "1998", "s": 4.807, "e": 5.464, "sm": 4807, "em": 5464, "cs": 68, "ce": 72, "si": 0}, {"i": 14, "w": "to", "s": 5.464, "e": 5.793, "sm": 5464, "em": 5792, "cs": 73, "ce": 75, "si": 0}, {"i": 15, "w": "2005", "s": 5.793, "e": 6.45, "sm": 5792, "em": 6450, "cs": 76, "ce": 80, "si": 0}, {"i": 16, "w": ",", "s": 6.45, "e": 6.8, "sm": 6450, "em": 6800, "cs": 80, "ce": 81, "si": 0}, {